  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <div class="accordion edtech-faq" id="edtechFaq">
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq2">Can you integrate with our existing Student Information System (SIS)?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We integrate with major SIS platforms including PowerSchool, Infinite Campus, Skyward, and others, and can build custom integrations for proprietary systems.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq3">How do you ensure FERPA/COPPA compliance?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We build privacy and security into the architecture from day one: data encryption, access controls, audit logging, parental consent workflows. We also provide compliance documentation and training.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq4">Can the platform handle thousands of concurrent users?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We design for scale using cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure) with auto-scaling. We've built platforms that handle 100,000+ concurrent users during peak times.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq5">What about accessibility for students with disabilities?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We follow WCAG 2.1 AA and Section 508, including screen reader support, keyboard navigation, captions for videos, and alternative text. Accessibility is tested throughout development.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq6">Can instructors create their own content?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We build intuitive course authoring tools so instructors can create and manage content without technical expertise, multimedia, quizzes, assignments, and interactive elements.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq8">Do you provide ongoing support and maintenance?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We offer support packages including bug fixes, security updates, feature enhancements, and technical support, plus training for your team to manage the platform independently.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq9">Can you help with content migration from our old system?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We provide data migration services to transfer courses, user data, grades, and content from legacy systems, ensuring data integrity and minimal disruption.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#edfaq10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="edfaq10">How do you measure the success of an EdTech platform?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="edfaq10" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#edtechFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">We focus on measurable outcomes: student engagement, course completion rates, learning outcomes, instructor time savings, administrative efficiency, and user satisfaction scores.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

